{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>O house of Jacob, come and let us walk</b> etc. These are the words of the prophet reproving Israel, and the meaning is: after you know that Zion shall be redeemed now through justice, and yet a time of great salvation for her will still come, we are obligated that we all believe in the words of prophecy, which are true as light. And the prophet included himself among them by way of admonition, as Moses said, <i>and pardon our iniquity</i> (Exodus 34:9) — or because he grew up with them and learned from the ways of their speech, as I shall explain:"], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:52:23.202252563Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}